  "description": "Kang Rak-Won, the CEO of a planning company who started out as an idol, hears the news of the suicide of Lee Do-Woon, who used to be in the same team. Ten years ago, Team Delight was disbanded due to Do-Woon's betrayal, so Rak-Won attends the funeral with mixed feelings. Rak-Won takes a short nap at the funeral. When he wakes up, he has returned to the past 20 years ago. However, the members are already slightly out of sync.\n\n *\"Everything is so easy for you, hyung.\"\n\"Do it without me. I don't want to sing.\"\n\"I don't even have that much skill... It's ridiculous. The song I wrote.\"* \n\nRak-Won fights to prevent the team's disbandment and Lee Do-Woon's suicide. The story of three dogs with different owners and servants regaining their idol status.\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)\n\n*Note: Includes ten extra chapters.*",
